# Questions and answers for the FAQ section on this page (see pages/index.faq).
Q: Do you demolish houses, garages and outbuildings?
A: Yes. We carry out full and partial structural demolition of residential, commercial and industrial buildings, including garages, outbuildings, barns and slabs, for property owners clearing a lot for sale, redevelopment or a new build.

Q: Can you do interior or selective demolition in an occupied building?
A: Yes. We carry out interior strip-outs in occupied buildings and work alongside live utilities and neighbouring structures.

Q: What does site clearance include after demolition?
A: Slab, footing and foundation removal, grubbing, stump and vegetation clearance, backfill, compaction and rough grading, and erosion and sediment control measures, leaving a parcel a surveyor and a builder can both work from.

Q: Can salvage reduce the cost of demolition?
A: Yes. Structural steel, non-ferrous metals, equipment, fixtures and architectural salvage are recovered and sold rather than dumped, and the value comes off your invoice. We can also provide recycling records for LEED or client reporting.

Q: Who does Beltway Demolition work for?
A: Property owners, general contractors, commercial and industrial clients, and municipal and institutional clients across Maryland, Washington DC and Virginia.
